HST Office: Format Cells in Sheets follows Excel: tabs Number, Alignment, Font, Border, Fill, Protection
(owner-approved Microsoft Office parity for beta.5).

- Tab order as in Excel; the Background page is labelled "Tô màu" here only. Page ids stay, so
  .uno:FormatCellDialog and other callers that open a page by id keep working.
- Alignment has "Gộp ô" (Merge cells): on for one merged block, mixed when the selection only contains
  merged cells, unavailable for one plain cell. OK merges or unmerges the selection. Other users of the
  page (cell styles, dbaccess) leave SID_TABLE_MERGE_CELLS out of the item set and do not see it.
- Number lists its categories in Excel's order in Sheets and adds "Kế toán" (Accounting): decimals and a
  symbol only, with the symbol and digits aligned by a fill, four sections like Excel's code. A cell with
  such a format reopens on that row, also when it came from .xlsx. Other documents keep the old list.

- Font holds the effects (hst-dlg-font.patch); .uno:FontEffectsDialog opens that tab. Cell styles keep their tabs.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-sheets.py (format-cells-tabs, merge-cells, accounting).
